== Other Stuff

=== The 3 Models of Computation

There are apparently 3 seperate models of computation which all act slightly differently.

_Boolean circuits_ with fixed input that focus only on depth. (Massive parallelizm is allowed). Computational classes are $A C$, $N C$ etc. People mess with these by adding different special gates and proving things with these new special gates added.

_Turing Machine_ which notably has an $O(n)$ array indexing speed. (and takes an unlimited size word $x$ as input). This has interesting consequences like time-memory of algorithms being related. For example PSPACE class contains NP space etc. algorithms.

_RAM model_ what we know as normal computer with fast array indexing.

It would appear that our computers differ from these mathematical models. Certain operations are clearly faster, others are slower than some of these models.
